687
00:54:42,380 --> 00:54:45,100
Rym: But otherwise, I highly recommend you play Slay This Princess.

688
00:54:45,646 --> 00:54:46,999
Rym: Otherwise, we will see you at PAX West.

689
00:54:47,620 --> 00:54:56,999
Rym: And so tonight, I leave you with... Bitzy, you told us that your town was going to kick you out forever, and you don't even seem upset about that.

690
00:54:57,480 --> 00:55:05,015
Emily: They keep asking me to leave, and I didn't leave, and then they were going to tell me to kick out, and then I was going to be kicked out, and I was like, I don't want that to happen.

691
00:55:06,741 --> 00:55:08,399
Rym: Why were they going to kick you out?

692
00:55:08,920 --> 00:55:12,060
Emily: Because they don't understand the difference between lemons and lemon juice.

693
00:55:13,994 --> 00:55:14,120
Emily: What?

694
00:55:14,362 --> 00:55:16,140
Emily: It's a long story, you wouldn't understand.

695
00:55:17,364 --> 00:55:18,080
Emily: I'm really trying.

696
00:55:18,520 --> 00:55:27,220
Emily: If they had to kick you out because they didn't understand the difference between lemons and lemon juice, we might have to kick you out if we don't understand the difference between lemons and lemon juice.

697
00:55:27,500 --> 00:55:30,960
Rym: Well, the one is the lemon, and then the other's like a liquidy juice type.

698
00:55:31,180 --> 00:55:39,720
Emily: They kept saying that one came from the other, and that's f***ing horsesh*t. Clearly the juice comes from the lemon, but once you squeeze the juice out of the lemon, it hence, it stops being a lemon.

699
00:55:39,740 --> 00:55:42,279
Emily: This is what they kept saying, that doesn't make any sense.

700
00:55:42,460 --> 00:55:46,199
Emily: I don't have any lemons on me, but if you squeeze that lemon and lemon juice, I wouldn't.

701
00:55:48,421 --> 00:55:51,200
Rym: All right, when we get to click clock, I am going to blow your mind.

